.\" Generated by "sysml-mcp -man"; edit the description in the command's usage.go.
.TH SYSML-MCP 1 "2026-08-30" "OpenSysML" "OpenSysML Manual"
.SH NAME
sysml\-mcp \- Model Context Protocol server for SysML v2 and KerML
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sysml\-mcp
[options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
sysml\-mcp serves OpenSysML to coding agents over the Model Context Protocol,
as tools an agent calls: the language server's diagnostics, navigation,
editing and rendering over the model documents under the workspace root; the
runtime's one\-shot parsing, evaluation, instantiation, execution,
verification, querying and conversion; and named REPL sessions whose
declarations, instances and runs persist across calls; the protocol is spoken
over stdin/stdout, so an agent host starts this server rather than a shell.
.PP
The documents under the root are managed as one workspace, so a declaration in
one resolves against the others, and the standard library is the copy embedded
in this binary unless OPENSYSML_LIBRARY_PATH names another.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-cache\-size " int"
Maximum number of parsed models the runtime tools hold; at least 1. The
default is 100.
.TP
.B \-h
Show this help (shorthand)
.TP
.B \-help
Show this help and exit
.TP
.BI \-log\-level " string"
Lowest level logged to stderr: debug, info, warn or error. The default is
warn.
.TP
.B \-man
Write this command's manual page, in roff, to stdout and exit
.TP
.B \-no\-record\-cache
Parse every document and hold it loaded, reading no interface record from the
record cache and writing none; default off, or OPENSYSML_RECORD_CACHE=0
.TP
.BI \-root " string"
Workspace folder whose model documents the server indexes and edits; default
the current directory, which an agent host sets to the project. The default is
\&..
.TP
.B \-stdio
Serve over stdin/stdout (the only transport; accepted for hosts that name it)
.TP
.B \-strict
Serve strict conformance from the start: notation no pinned SysML v2
production admits is an error
.TP
.BI \-tools " string"
Tool groups to serve, comma\-separated: lsp (diagnostics, navigation, editing,
rendering), runtime (one\-shot evaluation, execution, verification,
conversion), session (persistent REPL sessions); default all. The default is
all.
.TP
.B \-v
Show version (shorthand)
.TP
.B \-version
Show version information
.SH STARTING THE SERVER
.RS 2
.nf
# What an agent host runs, in the project directory
sysml\-mcp
# Serve the models under another folder
sysml\-mcp \-root models
# Serve without persistent sessions
sysml\-mcp \-tools lsp,runtime
.fi
.RE
.PP
An agent host declares the server in its configuration, as {"mcp": {"sysml":
{"type": "local", "command": ["sysml\-mcp"]}}} in OpenCode's opencode.json,
and starts it with the project as the working directory.
.SH TOOLS
The tools, by the group that serves them (\-tools), each with the sysml\-grpc
RPC or sysml flag it stands for. The tool_catalog tool answers this list to
the client, narrowed to the groups served.
.TP
.B tool_catalog
every group: List the tools this server serves, each with the RPC or sysml
flag it stands for.
.TP
.B workspace_info
lsp: Describe the workspace root and the documents it holds, with their
diagnostic counts.
.TP
.B apply_edits
runtime: Apply workspace edits to a parsed model and answer the edited
documents (rpc ApplyEdits).
.TP
.B convert
runtime: Convert a model between the textual notation, JSON, RDF and XMI (rpc
Convert, sysml \-convert, sysml \-from, sysml \-id).
.TP
.B diagnostics
runtime: Report every diagnostic of a parsed model, as sysml \-validate does
(rpc GetDiagnostics, sysml \-validate).
.TP
.B explain_diagnostic
runtime: Explain a diagnostic code, or list every code with its summary (sysml
\-explain).
.TP
.B evaluate
runtime: Evaluate an expression against a parsed model (rpc Evaluate, sysml
\-eval).
.TP
.B evaluate_calc
runtime: Evaluate a calculation definition or usage (rpc EvaluateCalc, sysml
\-calc).
.TP
.B execute_action
runtime: Execute an action with bound inputs and report its outputs (rpc
ExecuteAction, sysml \-action, sysml \-schedule).
.TP
.B execute_state
runtime: Run a state machine over a sequence of events and report the trace
(rpc ExecuteState, sysml \-state).
.TP
.B export_graphs
runtime: Export the lowered action and state graphs of a model (rpc
ExportGraphs, sysml \-graphs).
.TP
.B instantiate
runtime: Instantiate a definition or usage and report the object's feature
values (rpc Instantiate, sysml \-instantiate).
.TP
.B list_engines
runtime: List the analysis engines and whether each is ready (rpc ListEngines,
sysml \-engines).
.TP
.B migrate
runtime: Migrate a SysML v1 model to SysML v2 and report what moved (rpc
Migrate, sysml \-migrate, sysml \-migration\-report, sysml
\-migration\-results, sysml \-layout, sysml \-image\-base\-url).
.TP
.B parse
runtime: Parse files or inline sources and answer the roots, diagnostics and a
model hash (rpc ParseFile, rpc ParseSources, sysml \-strict).
.TP
.B query
runtime: Run an OSLC query against a parsed model (rpc Query, sysml \-query).
.TP
.B render_model_document
runtime: Render a document definition as Markdown or HTML (rpc RenderDocument,
sysml \-render\-document, sysml \-doc\-form).
.TP
.B record_run
runtime: Run an analysis case and record the runs into the model as
AnalysisRecords declarations (rpc RecordRun, sysml \-record\-run, sysml
\-record\-into).
.TP
.B render_model_view
runtime: Render a view as its nodes, edges and compartments (rpc RenderView,
sysml \-render, sysml \-render\-ports, sysml \-render\-show, sysml
\-render\-depth).
.TP
.B run_analysis
runtime: Run an analysis case and report its result (rpc RunAnalysis, sysml
\-analysis, sysml \-engine).
.TP
.B run_document_query
runtime: Run a document query definition and report its rows (rpc
RunDocumentQuery, sysml \-run\-query).
.TP
.B run_runs
runtime: Run an action or a Monte Carlo case repeatedly and table what the
runs observed (rpc RunRuns, sysml \-runs, sysml \-observe).
.TP
.B run_sweep
runtime: Run an analysis case over ranges of its parameters (rpc RunSweep,
sysml \-sweep).
.TP
.B self_check
runtime: Apply the reflective SysMLValidation constraints to every element of
a model (rpc SelfCheck, sysml \-self\-check, sysml \-self\-check\-package).
.TP
.B server_info
runtime: Report the service version and the capabilities it serves (rpc
GetServerInfo).
.TP
.B symbol
runtime: Describe one element of a parsed model (rpc GetSymbol).
.TP
.B validate_instance
runtime: Validate an instantiated object against its definition, as sysml
\-validate=<object> does (rpc ValidateInstance).
.TP
.B verify_constraint
runtime: Verify a constraint and answer the verdict (rpc VerifyConstraint,
sysml \-constraint).
.TP
.B verify_requirement
runtime: Verify a requirement and answer the verdict (rpc VerifyRequirement,
sysml \-requirement).
.TP
.B verify_satisfaction
runtime: Verify a satisfy relationship and answer the verdict (rpc
VerifySatisfaction, sysml \-satisfy).
.TP
.B session_close
session: Close an open REPL session.
.TP
.B session_list
session: List the open REPL sessions.
.TP
.B session_open
session: Open a REPL session over a workspace and answer its id.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The status reports how the session ended:
.TP
.B 0
The protocol was served to its end: the client closed the stream, or the
process was told to stop.
.TP
.B 1
The server could not start, or the session ended in a protocol error.
.TP
.B 2
The command line could not be acted on.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_LIBRARY_PATH
Directory to load the SysML/KerML standard library from, instead of the copy
embedded in the binary.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_LIBRARY_ROOTS
Directories, separated as PATH is, to look for installed projects under when a
loaded file belongs to a project (a directory holding .project.json), besides
the project's own well\-known library directory (.sysand/lib).
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_STEPS
Expression evaluations one run may spend before it is reported as a runaway.
Default 10000000.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_ACTION_STEPS
Token\-flow steps one action run may perform. Default 1000000.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_EVENTS
Events one state machine run may dispatch. Default 1000000.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_DO_STEPS
Do actions one state machine run may perform. Default 5000000.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_ELEMENTS
Collection elements one evaluation may hold, which bounds the memory a run
holds rather than the work it does. Default 1000000.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_CALC_DEPTH
Nested calc invocations one run may hold on the stack, which is what a
recursion spends. Default 10000, ceiling 25000.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_SWEEP_RUNS
Runs one parameter sweep or sample may make, each a whole analysis or calc run
of its own with its own budgets. Default 1000.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_INTEGER_BITS
Bits the magnitude of one Integer a run computes may take; Integers are
otherwise unbounded, and a result past it, such as a large power, is refused
before it is computed. At least 64, so every machine\-word Integer fits;
default 1048576.
.PP
Each variable above also answers to its legacy SYSML_\-prefixed name
(SYSML_MAX_STEPS for OPENSYSML_MAX_STEPS, and so on), which remains accepted.
When both are set and the OPENSYSML_ value is non\-empty, the OPENSYSML_ value
wins; setting only the legacy name prints a one\-time deprecation warning on
standard error.
.PP
A budget bounds one run \(em one evaluation, one instantiation, one calc
invocation, one action, one state machine \(em not a whole session, so a long
session of small operations never exhausts one. A run started inside another
shares the outer run's budget.
